# The shim snapshots every file in the engine's directory, so each capture carries
# copies of EZNEC's own housekeeping state. Those are not evidence of the protocol
# and would triple the file count; the pre/post manifests still record their sizes
# and SHA-256s, so nothing is lost by leaving the copies untracked.
#
# What IS tracked: the deck EZNEC wrote (EZN5.NEC), the printout it read back
# (NEC5.OUT), the stdio tees, the manifests, and meta.tsv.
*__EZNEC.INI
*__LastZ*.txt
*__LastZ*.s1p

# (LastRun.log copies are already covered by the repo-root *.log rule.)
